REM dhancha — stand up a dockerised lab for one collaborator domain
CYCLER "lab"
TITLE "A laboratory for your own work"
OUTPUT KIND LAB
RESOLUTION EASY

STAGE CONCEPT
  VERB CREATE
  SHAPE TEXT
  ASK <<
    Name the domain, and the ONE piece of your own regular work this lab has to serve
    on the first day. Not the research programme — the thing on your desk this week.
    A lab justified only by what it might enable later is a lab nobody switches on.
    Then name what you already have: the machine, the instruments, the licences.
  >>
  EXPECT TEXT
  VALIDATE "names one real piece of the collaborator's own work"
END STAGE

STAGE ENABLEMENT
  VERB CREATE
  SHAPE LIST
  ASK <<
    List what the stack actually gives this domain, layer by layer, and for each item say
    which of the collaborator's tasks it touches.
    Then list what it does NOT give them, and what they will still need elsewhere.
    An enablement list with nothing absent on it has not been thought about.
  >>
  EXPECT LIST
END STAGE

STAGE COMPONENTS
  VERB INTEGRATE
  SHAPE LIST
  ASK <<
    Which Humanesque components does this domain genuinely use? Not every domain gets
    every component. For each one you include, name the task it serves; a component with
    no named task comes out.
    Do not equate a component with a pipeline, and do not make one component the parent
    of another.
  >>
  EXPECT LIST
END STAGE

STAGE BOM
  VERB MEASURE
  SHAPE DATA
  ASK <<
    Price layers 0 and 1. Every row carries the part, the quantity, the price, the
    currency, the SOURCE and the time you retrieved it.
    A row you cannot price stays unpriced, and the total stays Unknown. Do not quote a
    total over the priced rows — that reads as the cost of the build.
  >>
  EXPECT DATA
END STAGE

STAGE GRAIL
  VERB CREATE
  SHAPE TEXT
  ASK <<
    Instantiate the loop for this domain: research, formalisation, simulation, prototype,
    experiment, instrumentation, observation, evidence, verification, revision.
    For each step say what the artifact is HERE. A step whose artifact you cannot name is
    a step this lab does not yet close.
    Then state the rung each of this domain's current claims enters at.
  >>
  EXPECT TEXT
END STAGE

STAGE FALSIFY
  VERB FALSIFY
  SHAPE TEXT
  ASK <<
    What would make a collaborator abandon this lab in week two? Name the dependency that
    will not install, the instrument driver that does not exist, the licence they do not
    have, the dataset that is not public.
    Report what you found, not that you looked.
  >>
  EXPECT TEXT
END STAGE

STAGE HANDOVER
  VERB VERIFY
  SHAPE TEXT
  ASK <<
    Run: docker compose build, then the lab's own check.
    Paste the output. Then state the three lists: what runs, what is wired but unproven,
    what is not built. An empty list is a valid answer; a missing list is not.
  >>
  EXPECT TEXT
  GATE "LAB ready"
END STAGE
